# The ENV page (a tap of ENV: held with a black key it is still the minor row). KNOB 1 and 2 are the
# strings' attack and release, KNOB 3 and 4 the chord and bass's; the four are the project's, so SAVE
# keeps them. Attack linear, release exponential, 0 ms .. 10 s on a geometric knob.
wait 300
tap ENV
wait 200
expect view 6
expect par16 0                    # Str A: a fresh FM-1 plucks as it always did
expect par17 100              # Str R: 10 s, so the natural decay ends the string first
expect par18 0                    # Chd A
expect par19 42               # Chd R: the 0.18 s the chord had
shot env-default.png
# a chord with a long attack: quiet at once, loud a second later; and with a long release it rings on
spin K3 70
wait 100
expect par18 70
spin K4 30
wait 100
expect par19 72
shot env-long.png
key b1 down
wait 25
expect chord_level <40
wait 900
expect chord_level >60
key b1 up
wait 60
expect chord_level >20          # the release rings on
wait 700
shot env-tail.png
# the strings: a slow attack means the level is low just after the pluck
spin K3 -70
wait 80
spin K1 60
wait 80
expect par16 60
key w6 down
wait 20
expect strlevel6 <40
key w6 up
wait 300
# the four times are saved with the project (SAVE, and the settings' autosave)
tap SAVE
wait 100
expect dirty 0
reboot
wait 300
expect par16 60
expect par17 100
expect par18 0
expect par19 72
tap ENV
wait 200
shot env-after-reboot.png
# the screen reader hears the page: the four times, in the words file's own words
listen
wait 100
where
said Env page: Str A 614 ms, Str R 10.0s, Chd A 0 ms, Chd R 1.4s
